cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this firmware, please cite the paper listed in preferred-citation."
title: "Battery-Free Wireless Torque Sensor (BWTS): Demo Firmware"
abstract: >-
  Firmware for a battery-free wireless torque-sensing platform based on the
  Texas Instruments CC430F5137. It contains a sensor node that samples a
  strain-gauge bridge and transmits the reading over a sub-1 GHz radio link,
  and a receiver node that forwards the received value over UART. This
  repository accompanies the paper "Battery-Free Wireless Torque Sensor
  Powered by RF Energy" (IEEE Internet of Things Journal, 2023).
